-$$ V = C_{00}C_{11} - C_{10}C_{01} - I(C_{00} + C_{11} - C_{10} - C_{01}) $$
-
-**Decision Logic:**
-1.  If $V < 0$: The isocontour forms a rectangular hyperbola in the first and third quadrants relative to the saddle point. The connectivity connects the vertices with the same sign as $C_{00}$ and $C_{11}$ (diagonal 0-2) [S4].
-2.  If $V > 0$: The isocontour forms a rectangular hyperbola in the second and fourth quadrants. The connectivity connects the vertices with the same sign as $C_{10}$ and $C_{01}$ (diagonal 1-3) [S4].
+2.  **Determine Connectivity:**
+    *   If $V < 0$ (or $Q < 0$), the isocontour forms a rectangular hyperbola in the first and third quadrants (relative to the center of the face). This implies that the corners $(0,0)$ and $(1,1)$ are connected, and $(0,1)$ and $(1,0)$ are connected [S4][S6, unofficial].
+    *   If $V > 0$ (or $Q > 0$), the isocontour forms a rectangular hyperbola in the second and fourth quadrants. This implies that the corners $(0,1)$ and $(1,0)$ are connected, and $(0,0)$ and $(1,1)$ are connected [S4][S6, unofficial].
 
